# VoiceVision Feature: Speaker Identification (T034)
# Source: src/voicevision/backends/speaker.py

## SimpleSpeakerBackend
- Session-based speaker tracking (not persistent across sessions)
- Audio features: RMS energy, zero-crossing rate, spectral centroid approximation
- Cosine similarity matching with configurable threshold (default 0.75)
- Max 10 speakers per session

## Features Extracted
- RMS energy: normalized 0.0-1.0
- Zero-crossing rate: crossings per sample
- Spectral centroid approx: high-frequency energy ratio (simple FFT alternative)

## Algorithm
- Extract features from utterance audio
- Compare with existing speaker profiles (average features)
- If similarity >= 0.75: match existing speaker
- Else: create new speaker (Speaker 1, Speaker 2, ...)
- Min utterance duration: 0.5s (configurable)

## PipelineConfig.speaker_enabled
- Default: False
- Env: VOICEVISION_SPEAKER=1

## Pipeline.process()
- Resets speaker backend at start of each session
- Runs identify() on each utterance
- Speaker label available but not yet used in output

## HTTP /transcribe
- When speaker_enabled: returns "speaker": "Speaker 1"

## VoicePipeline.detect_speaker(audio, sample_rate)
- Returns speaker label or None